## Caveats
- Several scale figures (Spotify Honk PR counts, Klarna FTE-equivalents, bank KYC/AML percentages) are company- or vendor-reported and not independently audited; treat as directional.
- The "seven requirements for production agents" framing is a third-party consultancy's synthesis of Cloudflare's platform, not an official Cloudflare list.
- Both zknill posts are authored by an Ably employee and end in product pitches; the technical analysis is sound, but the "HTTP is a bad transport" conclusion is contested (the Redis Streams counterview).
- MongoDB-checkpoint-at-scale and bank-specific agent-architecture evidence is thin (as you anticipated): the former rests on a handful of primary community reports; the latter on press/vendor material with little published architecture detail.
- Regulation is in active flux as of September 2026 (SR 11-7 → successor rescission April 2026; EU AI Act high-risk deadline Aug 2 2026 with a proposed but unenacted delay; FCA/MAS guidance pending).
